Avery,

Thank you for making the time on short notice. Two things from the call stayed with me. First, that your customers measure you against the schedule they would have run without you, not against a dashboard; that is a much harder bar and a better one. Second, that the procurement lead, not the plant manager, is the person who renews you. I would like to understand both more carefully.

Could we do a proper working session next week with Priya in the room? An hour would be plenty. I'd like to walk the architecture at the level a non-engineer can follow and then spend most of the time on how a plant goes from the first line to the second. Wednesday, March 4 at 2pm works on my side, as does Thursday morning.

One question in the meantime, since it will shape how I prepare: when a plant adds a second line, is that usually the same buyer signing again, or a new one?

Farah

